From 7c57dda811a1e5e30fed418827330015359ebeaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] web: speed-ramp block in the Recording format card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Why: speed ramping (T31) had only socket commands. Cinemate puts the same
controls on its web UI (SHUTTER SYNC and FPS DOUBLE toggles, the ramp
stepper); Patrik asked for a Cinemate-style section by expanding Format.
What: under Bit Depth in Settings > Record > Recording format:
- Speed Ramp On/Off (set_fps_ramp), disabled during a take because Core
  refuses to toggle it mid-take. The pill shows Off, On · Angle,
  On · Exposure or Ramping (fps_ramp_stepping).
- Shutter Sync: Angle keeps the motion blur, Exposure keeps the
  brightness (set_fps_ramp shutter=angle|exposure).
- Ramp to <fps> over Cut/1/2/5/10/20 s (ramp_fps to seconds). The targets
  are the FPS pills' list (availableFpsOptionsForSnapshot, so fpsPresets
  and the mode ceiling) without the current rate.
- ×2 ramps to twice the take's start rate (Cinemate FPS DOUBLE), greyed
  out above the highest selectable value; Back returns to the take's
  start rate, or outside a take to the rate before the last ×2.
- The note says when the format cannot ramp (H.264, ProRes, stills) and,
  in a take, the rate every frame is numbered at; one line gives the
  selectable range in the current mode.
Command replies and the optimistic snapshot patch carry fps_ramp and
fps_ramp_keep_exposure, so the pills follow at once.

Tested: host g++ -fsyntax-only; node --check on the page script; page
driven in Chromium against a mocked /api/state and /api/command: seven
states (4K Clear HDR 16-bit range 24-25 with ×2 greyed out, 2K SDR,
after ×2, recording at base 50, H.264 take, stepping), commands as
expected, no console errors, no horizontal scroll at 390 px. Not run
against Core on a Pi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T93jucKMhWYnQM1yyFVkbH
